docs/FACTS.md:244:| F-455 | 2026-11-12 | V (docs) | Vercel REST, change an existing project domain: `PATCH https://api.vercel.com/v9/projects/{idOrName}/domains/{domain}?teamId=<team id>`, `Authorization: Bearer <token>`, JSON body `{"redirect": "<target domain>" \| null, "redirectStatusCode": 301\|302\|307\|308\|null, "gitBranch": "<branch>" \| null}` ("Update a project domain's configuration, including the name, git branch and redirect of the domain"). Error list includes `400` "The domain redirect is not valid". Adding a domain: `POST /v10/projects/{idOrName}/domains` with the same `redirect` / `redirectStatusCode` fields. Doc examples send `"redirectStatusCode": "307"` as a string while the schema says `integer` → send the integer `308`. Dashboard equivalent: Project Settings → Domains → **Edit** → **Redirect to**, available "when more than one domain is present in the project" | https://vercel.com/docs/rest-api/projects/update-a-project-domain.md (last_updated 2026-11-12; l.19,22,50-78,263-265); https://vercel.com/docs/rest-api/projects/add-a-domain-to-a-project.md (l.19,70-83); https://vercel.com/docs/domains/working-with-domains/deploying-and-redirecting.md (last_updated 2026-08-11; l.55,61) | WO-62b, orchestrator (vercel.app → 308) |
